From 50e7ffe307cc7afdaf85275b559fa9e79503a096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:21:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Time capsule: show only the towers completed by a chosen
 year, with a year slider and Play

A Time capsule button at the foot of the map opens a dock with the chosen year, a bar chart of
completions per year with a slider under it, and Play, which walks forward a year at a time. While it
is on, only completed towers with a completion year up to the chosen year are shown (the other filters
still apply; the status chips are paused), and rings mark the towers and clusters completed in that
year. The range runs from the earliest completion year in the data (1889) to this year, and the dock
opens at this year; ?year=1931 opens it at 1931. MapApp's asOf (null when off) is the hook for layers
that change with the year.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015bnz9afFBBGLBukuAQtLqe
